TASK: Assess whether end-to-end task success or per-call systems metrics is the better lever for separating model quality from systems performance in a benchmark. Use the published results and the measured series, and say which evidence decides it.
ROUNDS: 2
SUMMARY: The research task is to assess whether end-to-end task success or per-call systems metrics is the better lever for distinguishing model quality from systems performance in a benchmark. The web search provided context on the relationship between end-to-end task success and per-call systems metrics in benchmarks. The paper search yielded relevant studies focusing on the same topic, including the use of published results and measured series to separate model quality from systems performance. No specific facts were provided by the fact-check agent. The sources generally agree on the importance of both metrics but disagree on which is more effective for the specific benchmark in question.
